# One block, not two.
#
# This file used to open with a `/*` block carrying the Referrer-Policy and
# follow it with this one, and the node composed the two: every block whose
# pattern matched was applied, the later ones over the earlier. The locked
# Edge Canon standard lowers `_headers` with first-match semantics - one block
# answers a path, the first whose pattern matches - and a file with more than
# one block is refused at build (EC_ROUTING_SOURCE_UNREPRESENTABLE) rather
# than have one target compose the blocks and another not. So the stylesheet
# carries both headers from the one block that names it, and `/` carries
# neither.
#
# The Cache-Control: the stylesheet only ever changes when the version does,
# and a version is a whole new bundle, so a year is safe. This is what
# overrides the node's own default for an asset, which is "ask me again every
# time" because a bundle path is not content-addressed.
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
